    slug: "3d-paper-cutout-collage",
    title: "纸雕立体拼贴",
    titleEn: "3d Paper Cutout Collage",
    tagline: "A four-panel photo split collage arranged in a 2x2 grid, presenting four fully layered 3D paper cut-out dioramas.",
    taglineEn: "AI image prompt.",
    category: "other",
    engines: ["other"],
    difficulty: 3,
    prompt: "纸雕何必是平面的呢\n---\nA four-panel photo split collage arranged in a 2x2 grid, presenting four fully layered 3D paper cut-out dioramas.\nGLOBAL STYLE (crucial constraint): Every single element in the scene, from the background hills to the central characters and objects, must be constructed from multiple stacked layers of cut matte cardstock. The edges of these paper layers must be visible on all objects, defining their form and volume through layering, not solid sculpting. Soft, warm directional studio lighting casts realistic drop shadows, revealing the thickness and depth of the stacked paper layers everywhere.\nTop Left Panel: A forest scene where oversized mushrooms and tiny foxes are built from stacked paper layers.\nTop Right Panel: A terraced village where houses and hills are formed by stepped layers of paper.\nBottom Left Panel: Two small figures and a boat made of layered paper, floating on water made of concentric paper layers with layered lanterns.\nBottom Right Panel: A character and a large castle, both constructed from stacked paper layers, on a layered paper cliff.\nCOLOR PALETTE: Warm, cozy tones of moss green, amber yellow, terracotta orange, deep teal, and creamy white. Octane render, 8k, palpable layered texture. --ar 1:1 --stylize 300",
