    category: "other",
    engines: ["other"],
    difficulty: 3,
    prompt: "☯️ Yin-Yang Mirror\nWhen the story's duality is about coexistence rather than opposition, try this circular approach.\nOne prompt to visualize a story's duality through yin-yang design — two opposing aspects of [Subject] occupy interlocking halves of a circular emblem, viewed from 45° bird's-eye.\nSame narrative, contrasting realms. Symbolic objects echo across the boundary, hinting at what was lost or gained. Lighting, color, and architecture amplify the tension. Just name the story that deserves its opposing mirror.",
